convincing|persuasive|ADJECTIVE|giving strong reason to believe|Making something seem true or reasonable through clear reasons or evidence.|có sức thuyết phục|Her explanation of the missing payment was convincing.|Lời giải thích của cô ấy về khoản thanh toán bị thiếu có sức thuyết phục.|Used before a noun or after a linking verb; describes the strength of persuasion, not proof that a claim is true.|0
exercise|physical-activity|NOUN|activity for fitness|Physical activity done to improve or maintain health and fitness.|việc tập thể dục|A short walk gives me some exercise during my lunch break.|Một cuộc đi bộ ngắn giúp tôi vận động trong giờ nghỉ trưa.|Usually uncountable for physical activity in general; an exercise can name a particular movement.|0
exercise|work-out|VERB|do physical activity|To move your body as an activity intended to improve fitness.|tập thể dục|They exercise together in the park before breakfast.|Họ cùng tập thể dục trong công viên trước bữa sáng.|Intransitive in this sense; exercise a muscle is a related transitive construction.|1
exercise|practice-task|NOUN|task for practising|A task or activity designed to practise a skill or check understanding.|bài tập|The final exercise asks students to compare two short texts.|Bài tập cuối yêu cầu học sinh so sánh hai đoạn văn ngắn.|Countable; an exercise in writing or a grammar exercise specifies the skill being practised.|2
exercise|use-authority|VERB|use a right or ability|To put a right, power, or ability into use.|thực hiện quyền; vận dụng khả năng|Residents may exercise their right to question the proposal.|Cư dân có thể thực hiện quyền chất vấn đề xuất của mình.|Transitive; takes objects such as a right, authority, or judgment, rather than a person being trained.|3
law|rule|NOUN|rule established by authority|A rule established by a governing authority that people are required to follow.|luật; quy định pháp luật|The new law requires clearer labels on food packages.|Luật mới yêu cầu nhãn rõ ràng hơn trên bao bì thực phẩm.|Countable for a particular rule; uncountable for the legal system, as in obey the law.|0
law|legal-study|NOUN|study and profession of legal rules|The study or professional practice of legal rules and their application.|ngành luật|After studying law, Linh joined a small legal practice.|Sau khi học luật, Linh vào làm tại một văn phòng luật nhỏ.|Uncountable when naming the academic field; study law does not take an indefinite article.|1
participation|taking-part|NOUN|involvement in an activity|The act of taking part in an activity with other people.|sự tham gia|Participation in the workshop is open to all staff.|Tất cả nhân viên đều có thể tham gia hội thảo.|Uncountable; participation in names the activity, while participation by names the participants.|0
shelter|safe-place|NOUN|place offering protection|A place that protects people or animals from danger or bad weather.|nơi trú ẩn|The hikers found shelter in an empty barn during the storm.|Những người đi bộ đường dài tìm được nơi trú trong một nhà kho trống khi bão đến.|Uncountable for protection in general; a shelter can be a particular building or structure.|0
shelter|protect|VERB|protect from harm or weather|To give someone or something protection from a danger or harsh conditions.|che chở; bảo vệ|The high wall shelters the garden from strong winds.|Bức tường cao che chắn khu vườn khỏi gió mạnh.|Transitive shelter someone or something from; also intransitive when people shelter in a place.|1
